findings.finding:
My current finding is that the cyclicity condition \(KNK'B\) reduces to a single algebraic equation in the two shape‑parameters \(\lambda=\frac{BC}{BD}=F_{n+2}/F_n\) and the incircle‑radius ratio \(r= \frac{r_{\text{incircle}}}{BD}\).  Using coordinates with \(B=(0,0),\,C=(\lambda,0),\,D=(1,0)\) and the incircle centre \(I=(1,r)\) one obtains after eliminating the reflection point \(K'\) that the points \(K,N,K',B\) are concyclic iff  

\[
{\,\lambda^{5}r^{2}+\lambda^{5}+\lambda^{4}r^{4}-5\lambda^{4}+6\lambda^{3}r^{4}-8\lambda^{3}r^{2}+10\lambda^{3}
+2\lambda^{2}r^{6}-22\lambda^{2}r^{4}+14\lambda^{2}r^{2}-10\lambda^{2}
-11\lambda r^{6}+23\lambda r^{4}-9\lambda r^{2}+5\lambda+r^{8}+6r^{6}-8r^{4}+2r^{2}-1=0.}
\]

(denominator of the derived expression is non‑zero).  This single polynomial equation completely characterises all \(n\)-tastic triangles (the only remaining free parameter is \(r>0\)).  In the limit \(n\to\infty\) we have \(\lambda\to\phi^{2}=(3+\sqrt5)/2\); solving the above for \(\lambda=\phi^{2}\) yields the limiting value of \(r\) and thus the asymptotic constant \(\alpha\).
